= Attestation — Technical =

A verifiable attestation can be modeled as claim payload C plus issuer/attester identifier A, context and time metadata M, and a proof σ over a canonical representation. Verification checks σ and policy; semantic validation separately assesses evidence, issuer authority, freshness, revocation/status, and whether C supports the relying party's decision.

== Modeling / security cautions ==
* attestation ≠ truth
* attestation ≠ identity
* valid signature ≠ validated claim content

